css='''body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#192735;background:#f4f6f8;margin:0;line-height:1.5}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:32px 26px 60px}h1{font-size:32px;margin:8px 0}h2{font-size:23px;margin:34px 0 12px}h3{font-size:17px}p{max-width:1030px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#56697b}section,.box,details{background:white;border:1px solid #d9e1e7;border-radius:9px;padding:18px 22px;margin:16px 0}.reject{border-left:6px solid #b33347}.note{border-left:5px solid #dd9c36;background:#fff9e9}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px}th,td{padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #e0e6eb;text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}th{background:#e9eff4}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}img{width:100%;height:auto}summary{font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer}.muted,small{color:#556776}a{color:#165b91}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px}.metric{font-size:27px;font-weight:bold}.negative{color:#a82d41}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:18px 12px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:25px}section,details{padding:12px}}'''
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>MAR — Sequential drift research — 26 October 2026</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main>', '<div class="eyebrow">MAR RESEARCH · 26 OCTOBER 2026 · MAR-SEQUENTIAL-DRIFT-01</div><h1>New strategy test: reject this rule</h1>', '<section class="reject"><b>It has not demonstrated an improvement over our strongest combination.</b><p>The candidate fails the preliminary economic test at baseline, moderate and desk costs. It will not advance to a funded portfolio comparison or paper deployment. The existing Cipher implementation work continues separately.</p><div class="grid"><div><small>2022–2025 net R · desk</small><div class="metric negative">'+f'{full.net_R:+.2f} R'+'</div></div><div><small>Mean net per $1,000 entry</small><div class="metric negative">'+f'{full.mean_net_pct:+.2f}%'+'</div></div><div><small>Trades · win rate</small><div class="metric">'+f'{int(full.trades)} · {full.win_pct:.1f}%'+'</div></div></div></section>', '<div class="box note"><b>Read the units carefully.</b> Each opportunity starts with $1,000 notional and fixed quantity. Different tokens overlap without a shared capital limit. These returns are average trade returns, not account ROI. R is net P&L divided by original price-stop risk. Opportunity drawdown is shown in R/USDT; no account drawdown percentage is claimed.</div>', '<p>The rule uses daily evidence of a directional change, scaled by past volatility. One unusually large day cannot trigger the bounded candidate alone. The comparison uses the same detector without that cap. Parameters were frozen before results; no winning-token list, parameter sweep or holding-time cap was used.</p>',img(chart)]
parts+=['<h2>Results by year and overall</h2><p><b>Desk cost: 0.31% per leg, approximately 0.62% per round trip.</b> The table attributes complete trade outcomes to their entry year. Calendar P&L separately marks positions across year boundaries.</p>']
cols=['period','trades','mean_net_pct','net_R','win_pct','profit_factor','calendar_net','opportunity_drawdown_R']
rename={'period':'Period','trades':'Trades','mean_net_pct':'Mean trade net %','net_R':'Entry-cohort R','win_pct':'Win %','profit_factor':'Profit factor','calendar_net':'Calendar P&L USDT','opportunity_drawdown_R':'Calendar opportunity DD (R)'}
parts.append(table(desk.set_index('period').loc[periods].reset_index()[cols].rename(columns=rename)))
parts+=['<p class="muted">2024 can have negative entry-cohort R and positive calendar P&L: older positions were still gaining during that year. Much of that unrealized profit was surrendered in 2025. The calendar figures include carry-in positions; they do not describe only trades opened that year. Drawdowns reset their measurement peak at each displayed period, while positions continue.</p>','<h2>What failed: funding, loss severity, and surrendered gains</h2>']
costrow=full[['gross','slippage','fees','funding_cost','net']].to_frame().T.rename(columns={'gross':'Gross price P&L','slippage':'Slippage cost','fees':'Fees','funding_cost':'Net funding paid','net':'Net P&L'})
parts.append(table(costrow))
parts+=['<p>Gross price gains of <b>'+f'{full.gross:,.2f}'+'</b> USDT were outweighed by <b>'+f'{full.funding_cost:,.2f}'+'</b> USDT of net funding payments, plus fills and fees. This is more specific than saying trading costs were too high. The primary rule produced many small losses and a few very large price moves; fixed stops and waiting for opposite evidence left some positions open for years.</p>', '<p>In this simulation, one long BONK opportunity began with $1,000 notional, stayed open about 800 days, and paid about $25,133 funding as its marked position value expanded. Its gross price gain of about $22,729 became a net loss of about $2,481. Funding is computed on the changing marked notional, not the original $1,000. There is no leverage or capital-account claim here.</p>']
parts.append(table(pd.DataFrame([{'Win rate %':full.win_pct,'Average winner USDT':full.average_win,'Average loser USDT':full.average_loss,'Median holding days':full.duration_median_days,'Closed-only net USDT':full.closed_net,'Terminal marks':full.terminal,'Data censors':full.data_censors}])))
parts+=['<p>The primary later-period mean R is negative, but block-bootstrap confidence intervals cross zero. The result supports rejecting this exact specification; it does not prove every sequential detector or every token is unprofitable.</p>','<h2>All central costs and the control</h2>']
parts.insert(-1, '<p>Direction matters: longs generated about $35,493 gross but ended at −$239 net; shorts lost about $18,023 net. Funding consumed the long gains while the short entries also lacked gross profitability. A funding-aware exit therefore cannot be assumed to solve every source of loss. Both directions remain in the follow-up specification. Win rates and profit factors here include marked terminal/censored outcomes; closed-only net is reported separately.</p>')
